        "original_id": "391abe4c-9d57-5c9a-b8ab-1f4dc7b41cd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: London Avenue Canal, New Orleans, Louisiana, Lake Pontchartrain, 7th Ward, Gentilly, Lakefront, El Paso, Rio Grande, New Mexico, Texas\n- Systems: Riverside Canal, diversion dam, irrigation project, drainage canal, flood walls, earthen levees\n- Events: Hurricane Katrina\n\nFacts:\n- The London Avenue Canal is a drainage canal in New Orleans, Louisiana, that pumps rainwater into Lake Pontchartrain.\n- The London Avenue Canal runs through the 7th Ward of New Orleans from the Gentilly area to the Lakefront.\n- In 2005, the London Avenue Canal's flood walls built atop earthen levees breached on both sides during Hurricane Katrina.\n- The Riverside Canal and its diversion dam are the southernmost system on an irrigation project that extends along the Rio Grande in New Mexico and Texas.",
